lines=['# Native wide bootstrap: complete 32K milestone','',f"Decision: **{'retain the candidate' if retained else 'reject the candidate as an engine improvement'}** under the criteria fixed before measurement. This compares Rust `c7adfb22` with frozen accepted Rust `4ced6ee8`; it does not measure a DwarfStar advantage.",'',f"Median paired prefill latency changes by {pct(s['prefill_ms']['paired_ratio']['median']):+.3f}%. Steady decode changes by {pct(s['gen_steady_tps']['paired_ratio']['median']):+.3f}% and peak RSS by {pct(s['peak_rss_bytes']['paired_ratio']['median']):+.3f}%. The separate macOS peak-memory-footprint metric changes by {pct(foot['summary']['paired_ratio']['median']):+.3f}% (baseline {foot['summary']['baseline']['median']/2**30:.3f} GiB, candidate {foot['summary']['candidate']['median']/2**30:.3f} GiB). Every raw pair and both order subsets are retained below.",'','## Implementation and scope','','In this candidate, native continuation at overall frontiers up to 32K processes the layers-0/1/2 bootstrap in one 4,096-row batch per chunk instead of sixty-four 64-row calls. Initial prefix, 2K, legacy callers and overall frontiers above 32K keep their existing schedules. Position arrays cover the larger batch; diagnostic raw-ring snapshots retain the final 128 rows. No shader arithmetic changes. Three complete source files restore byte-for-byte to 4ced6ee8 by reversing the recorded edits; the other 39 pinned sources are unchanged.','','The first candidate, 7b4b76ac, failed its first 12K internal gate at chunk 4096, layer 0 final HC; every initial prefix layer was exact. Its later correctness and timing runs did not execute. Inspection found four router launches with 4,096 threads per group although both compiled pipelines permit only 1,024. The repaired candidate uses MIN(rows,256) for those four launches, preserving short widths. The actual unchanged Metal kernels pass 29,344 output-word comparisons and 96 guards at 32/64/4,096 rows. The repaired full-model checks subsequently pass the original failure site and all remaining gates. The first compile-only failure and first model failure are preserved.','','## Correctness and diagnostic selection','','All 320 release host tests pass. Forced native release build, formatting, executable/source freeze, complete inverse-edit proof and final full model/prompt/oracle/binary/source hashes pass. The 12K internal run checks all 43 layers of the initial prefix and both native continuation chunks. Separate normal and profiled 32K/128 C0 runs each check all 16,677,120 FP32 logit words. The fresh baseline profile checks the same full output, making 50,031,360 FP32 logit-word comparisons across these three full runs. Token agreement alone is not C0.','',f"Strict counter audits validate every attention/tail packet, interval, order and attribution. Bootstrap-ingress recorded GPU time changes from {sel['baseline_target_ms']/1000:.3f}s to {sel['candidate_target_ms']/1000:.3f}s: raw ratio {sel['raw_aggregate_ratio']:.6f}, control-normalized ratio {sel['control_normalized_aggregate_ratio']:.6f}. Both meet the prospectively fixed <0.90 diagnostic gate. This is selection evidence; whole-engine results come from the separate unprofiled runs.",'','## Whole-engine results','','Two fresh-process warm-ups are preserved and excluded. Five complete pairs use orders AB, BA, AB, BA, AB with fixed 32K input and 128 greedy steps. All 12 exact transcripts, raw engine metadata, timing-off checks, host observations and process exit records pass. No favorable early stopping or discretionary reruns.','','| Pair | Order | Baseline prefill s | Candidate prefill s | Prefill change | Steady decode change | RSS change |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
